---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const authorSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  "mainEntity": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "@id": "https://easternalignment.com/#sarah",
    "name": "Sarah",
    "jobTitle": "Metaphysics Enthusiast & Online Psychic Reading Reviewer",
    "description": "Self-taught practitioner of astrology, tarot, psychology, BaZi, and feng shui. Founder of Eastern Alignment — an independent review site helping people navigate the online psychic reading market.",
    "url": "https://easternalignment.com/about/",
    "knowsAbout": ["Astrology", "Tarot", "BaZi", "Feng Shui", "Psychology", "Online Psychic Readings"],
    "sameAs": [],
  }
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Sarah — Eastern Alignment Founder"
  description="Meet Sarah, a dedicated metaphysics enthusiast who has self-studied astrology, tarot, BaZi & feng shui since age 21. After years of exploring online psychic platforms firsthand, she built Eastern Alignment to help real seekers navigate this space."
  jsonLd={authorSchema}
  hreflangEs="https://easternalignment.com/es/acerca-de/"
>
  <div class="about-page section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'About' }]} />

      <header class="about-hero">
        <img src="/sarah-avatar.jpg" alt="Sarah — Founder of Eastern Alignment" class="about-avatar-lg" width="100" height="100" loading="lazy" />
        <h1>Hi, I'm Sarah</h1>
        <p class="about-subtitle text-muted">
          Metaphysics enthusiast, self-taught reader, and the person behind Eastern Alignment.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who I Am</h2>

        <p>I've been a dedicated metaphysics enthusiast for years. Starting at 21, I began self-studying <strong>astrology, tarot, psychology, and eventually BaZi (Chinese Four Pillars) and feng shui</strong> — not as a passing interest, but as a genuine, ongoing exploration that I return to in my free time again and again. Over the years, I've spent a lot of my spare hours diving deep into these different systems, cross-referencing ideas across traditions, and building a real working understanding of how these frameworks operate.</p>

        <p>I'm not a professional practitioner — I'm someone who genuinely loves this world and has put in the time to learn it from the inside.</p>

        <h2>How I Got Into Online Psychic Readings</h2>

        <p>About three years ago, I started exploring the world of <strong>online psychic readings</strong>. I was curious — as someone with a background in metaphysics, I wanted to see what the experience was actually like from the customer side. So I started booking sessions across different platforms and with different readers, spending my own money to see what was out there.</p>

        <p>I also spent a lot of time reading through the internet — forums, Reddit threads, review sites, community discussions — collecting as much real user experience as I could find. And what I discovered was a market that was, frankly, all over the place:</p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quality varies wildly.</strong> Some readers were genuinely impressive. Others were vague, generic, or worse — manipulative.</li>
          <li><strong>Useful information is scattered and scarce.</strong> Real reviews from real people are buried across dozens of corners of the internet, and most "review" sites are just ads wearing a different hat.</li>
          <li><strong>Nobody was doing the work.</strong> There was no single, trustworthy place where someone who actually understood these traditions was evaluating platforms and readers <em>before</em> people spent their money.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>That gap is why I built Eastern Alignment.</p>

        <h2>Why This Site Exists</h2>

        <p>I created Eastern Alignment to be the resource I wished existed when I started. A straightforward, honest site that helps people who are genuinely looking for online psychic reading services — whether it's their first time or they've been burned before — make better decisions before they spend.</p>

        <p>This isn't a marketing site pretending to be a review site. It's a small, independent project run by one person who cares about this space and wants to do it right.</p>

        <h2>How I Research & Review</h2>

        <p>Every review and guide on Eastern Alignment is built on a layered process that I've refined over time. The full details — including my <strong>weighted scoring framework</strong>, <strong>evidence classification system</strong>, <strong>7-step testing protocol</strong>, and <strong>editorial independence policy</strong> — are documented in the complete <a href="/methodology/"><strong>Methodology & Editorial Standards</strong></a> page. Here's the short version:</p>

        <ol>
          <li><strong>Direct platform testing</strong> — I create real accounts and pay with my own money. Nothing beyond the standard welcome offers any new client receives — no sponsored credits, no press accounts, no special treatment.</li>
          <li><strong>Multi-reader sampling</strong> — I don't judge a platform on one reader. I test across different specialties, price tiers, and communication formats to understand the platform's range.</li>
          <li><strong>Community research</strong> — I systematically gather and analyze real user experiences from forums, Reddit, review aggregators, and social communities — separating genuine signal from noise.</li>
          <li><strong>AI-assisted analysis</strong> — I use current AI tools to help process large volumes of public information efficiently, surface patterns in user sentiment, and catch things manual review might miss.</li>
          <li><strong>Metaphysical competency lens</strong> — Because I've studied these traditions myself for years, I can assess whether a reader's approach is actually coherent and skilled — not just whether they were friendly.</li>
          <li><strong>Ongoing updates</strong> — Platforms change, readers come and go, pricing shifts. I revisit and update my content when the evidence changes.</li>
        </ol>

        <p>The <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> also documents my <a href="/methodology/#scoring-framework">scoring dimensions and weights</a>, my <a href="/methodology/#evidence-standards">evidence level system (A/B/C/D)</a>, and <a href="/methodology/#limitations">the specific structural limitations</a> I acknowledge in my work. If you want to understand exactly how a score or recommendation was reached, that's where to look.</p>

        <h2>What We Publish — And What We Don't</h2>

        <p>I want to be transparent about an important editorial decision.</p>

        <p>To be completely honest, to avoid unnecessary legal headaches or potential retaliation, I will probably never publish a master "blacklist" of platforms or readers to avoid. But please don't mistake my silence for approval. As someone who deeply respects these traditions, I absolutely despise seeing them used for manipulation—whether that's through scare tactics, hidden billing traps, or emotional exploitation. What I can publish is the <a href="/red-flags/">catalogue of manipulative patterns I screen for</a>, which tells you more about how to protect yourself than any list of names would.</p>

        <p>As a general rule, <strong>I don't go out of my way to publish negative hit pieces.</strong> If a platform or reader doesn't meet my standards, I simply don't feature them. I don't recommend them, and I don't give them visibility on this site.</p>

        <p>That said, I want to be clear: <strong>the absence of a platform or reader from this site doesn't mean they're bad.</strong> It may simply mean I haven't had the time or budget to test them yet. Eastern Alignment is a one-person operation, and there are real limits to what I can cover at any given time. I'm working on expanding, but I'd rather publish nothing than publish something I haven't personally verified.</p>

        <h2>An Honest Word About Limitations</h2>

        <p>I've put a lot of effort into making my research methodology as rigorous as I can. I use structured analysis, draw on years of personal study across multiple metaphysical traditions, collect data from every relevant source I can find, and use AI tools to help process and synthesize information at scale. I genuinely try to give you the clearest, most reliable picture possible.</p>

        <p>But I want to be upfront: <strong>none of this can guarantee a perfect fit for every person in every situation.</strong> Metaphysical guidance is inherently personal. A reader who connects deeply with one person may not click with another. A platform that fits your needs today may not be the right choice six months from now with a different question.</p>

        <p>What I publish reflects my experience, my research, and my best honest judgment — not a universal guarantee. I can't promise that every recommendation will work perfectly for you. What I <em>can</em> promise is that I'll always tell you what I actually found — including the parts I'm uncertain about — and that I will never trade that honesty for anything.</p>

        <h2>Affiliate Links & How This Site Is Funded</h2>

        <p>Eastern Alignment contains affiliate links. If you sign up for a platform through one of my links, I may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. This is how I fund the site, the testing, and the ongoing research.</p>

        <p>The affiliate relationship <strong>does not influence my ratings, rankings, or recommendations.</strong> My scoring framework and evaluation criteria are <a href="/methodology/#scoring-framework">publicly documented</a> and fixed before testing begins — no platform can negotiate a higher score. I've rated platforms poorly that pay higher commissions, and enthusiastically recommended platforms with lower payouts. The only thing that matters to me is whether a service genuinely helps the people who use it.</p>

        <h2>Get in Touch</h2>

        <p>Have a question about a platform or reader I've reviewed? Found a factual error? Want to share your own experience? I read every message and take corrections seriously.</p>

        <p>If you're a deep-dive metaphysics enthusiast like me, feel free to reach out. I'm more than happy to share my behind-the-scenes notes and observations with you (just be warned, they are unfiltered and pretty messy!). However, for obvious reasons, I will not share this raw data with psychic platforms, commercial entities, or anyone with a financial stake in this industry.</p>

        <p>📧 <a href="mailto:sarah@easternalignment.com">sarah@easternalignment.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .about-avatar-lg {
    display: block;
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 20%;
    border: 3px solid var(--color-border-light);
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-6);
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    max-width: 480px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }
</style>
